e `nextGeneration` exists and signature matches; only a runtime assertion mismatch will occur Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: Expected length 4, received length 0 (hardcoded `[]` still returned) Correct\n\nResult: Test fails as expected — hardcoded `[]` doesn't satisfy this test, forcing real neighbor-counting logic.\n\n## Green -- implement real Game of Life neighbor-counting logic\n\nNow that we have a real behavioral test, implement the actual algorithm (still minimal but correct — no more hardcoding is viable)."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01N8v66J71GtRtFajPnxvESo","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"export type Cell = [number, number];\n\nfunction cellKey(x: number, y: number): string {\n  return `${x},${y}`;\n}\n\nfunction countLiveNeighbors(\n  x: number,\n  y: number,\n  liveSet: Set<string>\n): number {\n  let count = 0;\n  for (let dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx++) {\n    for (let dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++) {\n      if (dx === 0 && dy === 0) continue;\n      if (liveSet.has(cellKey(x + dx, y + dy))) count++;\n    }\n  }\n  return count;\n}\n\nexport function nextGeneration(liveCells: Cell[]): Cell[] {\n  const liveSet = new Set(liveCells.map(([x, y]) => cellKey(x, y)));\n  const candidates = new Set<string>();\n\n  for (const [x, y] of liveCells) {\n    for (let dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx++) {\n      for (let dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++) {\n        candidates.add(cellKey(x + dx, y + dy));\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  const result: Cell[] = [];\n  for (const key of candidates) {\n    const [xStr, yStr] = key.split(\",\");\n    const x = Number(xStr);\n    const y = Number(yStr);\n    const neighbors = countLiveNeighbors(x, y, liveSet);\n    const isAlive = liveSet.has(key);\n\n    if (isAlive && (neighbors === 2 || neighbors === 3)) {\n      result.push([x, y]);\n    } else if (!isAlive && neighbors === 3) {\n      result.push([x, y]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n","path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_06-08-45_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1