plied\n\nExtracted a shared `neighborsOf(x, y): Cell[]` helper that generates the 8 neighbor coordinates once. Both `countLiveNeighbors` and `nextGeneration` now call it instead of duplicating the nested-loop offset logic. Also switched the candidate collection from a `Set<string>` (requiring re-parsing keys back into numbers) to a `Map<string, Cell>`, removing the `key.split(\",\")` / `Number(...)` parsing step and its associated bindings.\n\n## After Mass (same regions)\n\n```\nneighborsOf: bindings 3 (x,y,neighbors) + assignment 1 (push) + loop 2 + conditional 1 + invocation 1 (push)\nMass = bindings(3) + assignments(6) + loops(10) + conditionals(4) + invocations(2) = 25\n\ncountLiveNeighbors (now): bindings 3 (x,y,liveSet) + invocations 3 (neighborsOf, filter, has/cellKey combined ~2) \nMass ≈ bindings(3) + invocations(2x2=4) = 7 (loop logic now lives in neighborsOf, not duplicated)\n\nnextGeneration candidate loop: bindings 2 (x,y) + invocations 2 (neighborsOf, set)\nMass ≈ bindings(2) + invocations(2x2=4) = 6\n\nCombined relevant mass ≈ 25 + 7 + 6 = 38\n```\n\nMass Change: **54 → 38** (Δ −16), while the neighbor-offset logic now exists in exactly one place.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Extracted duplicated neighbor-offset enumeration into a shared `neighborsOf` helper; replaced string-key parsing with a `Map<string, Cell>` to avoid re-deriving `[x, y]` from keys.\n**Mass Change**: ≈54 → ≈38 (Δ −16) for the affected regions\n**Naming**: No renames needed — `cellKey`, `countLiveNeighbors`, `nextGeneration` all still accurately describe their behavior.\n**Tests**: All 4 passing tests remain green (6 `it.todo` remain untouched)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_06-08-45_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation fil